with a few thoughts.

00:44:02.220 --> 00:44:05.130
So first of all, I think
a move to serverless,

00:44:05.130 --> 00:44:08.520
or an increase of serverless
in your production workloads,

00:44:08.520 --> 00:44:12.000
is an amazing opportunity to
actually redefine or define

00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:14.340
those as SLIs and SLOs.

00:44:14.340 --> 00:44:16.800
I think this is where you
focus on the developer,

00:44:16.800 --> 00:44:18.360
and this is where
you set, really,

00:44:18.360 --> 00:44:21.420
things that matter to
your business as things

00:44:21.420 --> 00:44:24.670
that you should be monitoring.

00:44:24.670 --> 00:44:26.697
The second step probably,
especially given

00:44:26.697 --> 00:44:28.780
the announcement that we've
made around Cloud Run,

00:44:28.780 --> 00:44:31.480
is trying to understand what
is the best cloud serverless

00:44:31.480 --> 00:44:32.943
tool for the job.

00:44:32.943 --> 00:44:34.360
If you'd like to
give us functions

00:44:34.360 --> 00:44:36.010
because functions
as service is really

00:44:36.010 --> 00:44:38.110
how you think you want to
build your applications,

00:44:38.110 --> 00:44:40.510
that's all good and fine.

00:44:40.510 --> 00:44:43.720
Maybe you'd like to have
something more granular,

00:44:43.720 --> 00:44:47.410
and maybe that's an application
made of multiple app modules.

00:44:47.410 --> 00:44:48.880
And that's App Engine.

00:44:48.880 --> 00:44:51.010
Maybe it's a
container because you

00:44:51.010 --> 00:44:53.982
want full freedom in
terms of what languages

00:44:53.982 --> 00:44:54.940
and frameworks you use.

00:44:54.940 --> 00:44:57.185
And that would
probably be Cloud Run.

00:44:57.185 --> 00:44:58.810
So spend a little
bit of time, probably

00:44:58.810 --> 00:45:00.670
in the sessions
describing and getting

00:45:00.670 --> 00:45:03.700
into the details of Cloud
Run, to understand which

00:45:03.700 --> 00:45:06.160
serverless tool is best
for the job, all of which

00:45:06.160 --> 00:45:10.510
come supported with
logging and monitoring.

00:45:10.510 --> 00:45:13.360
And then there are features in
App Engine such as the Cloud

00:45:13.360 --> 00:45:17.410
Debugger and other features
and in other products.

